sufficient certificate of failure for $\sigma$.


\section{Constructing and certifying the line projector}
Let a nonzero row $v$ span the simultaneous solution space
$vN=0$, $vB=v$, and suppose $s=vQv^{\mathsf T}\ne0$. Put
\[
 E=s^{-1}Qv^{\mathsf T}v.
\]
Writing $w=vQ$, symmetry of $Q$ gives $E=s^{-1}w^{\mathsf T}v$.
This is a nonzero outer product, so it has rank one and row image $\langle v\rangle$.
Moreover $vw^{\mathsf T}=s$, whence $E^2=E$, and
$QE^{\mathsf T}Q^{-1}=E$. The equations $B^*=B$, $N^*=-N$ give
$BQ=QB^{\mathsf T}$ and $NQ=-QN^{\mathsf T}$. Together with the two
row equations these imply $BE=EB=E$ and $NE=EN=0$.
The implementation also checks these equations directly, together with
commutation of $E$ with both saved projections.

